# Supplied presentation content

Create these four slides in this order for an audience interested in NASA's
surface-power decision. They are a text-only historical excerpt from Michael
Chappell's February 2025 NASA Moon to Mars Architecture workshop presentation:
https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/2025-ia-workshop-wp-mars-surface-power.pdf

The supplied material is deliberately limited to source page 1 text, page 2 text,
page 5's upper two technology lists, and page 13 text. Other source slides,
illustrations, logos and page 5's lower rationale table are outside this excerpt.
Do not retrieve or reconstruct them. This input selection is already made by the
author; preserve all the content below. The two category lists on slide 3 are
peers; struck-out entries are excluded technologies, not ordinary active choices.
The decision is already supplied. Keep the original qualifiers about initial
crewed missions. Do not add facts, headlines, labels or claims.

Source attribution (may be in a small visible footer): NASA · Michael Chappell ·
February 2025 · historical text excerpt. No NASA endorsement is implied.

## Slide 1 — source page 1

Title: Mars Surface Power

Michael Chappell
Deputy Mars Architecture Lead
Strategy and Architecture Office
NASA – ESDMD – SAO

February 2025
Moon to Mars Architecture Workshops

