+Verification performed
+
+- Parsed output/slide.html and compared each slide's audience content with inputs/brief.md after normalizing whitespace only.
+- Confirmed four direct article slides, the original order, all headings, useful speaker notes, all six exact struck-out entries, and the full initial-crewed-missions qualifier.
+- Confirmed the supplied Lys CSS, JavaScript and provenance notice are embedded, with no external script, font, image or stylesheet dependencies.
+- Validated the exact output/decision.json key set and protocol value.
+- Executed the shipped Lys runtime and reading-mode adapter in an offline Node DOM harness. Desktop and phone startup, ArrowLeft/ArrowRight/Home/End/Space handlers, navigation links, hidden-slide focus guards, reading-mode cleanup, resizing and print lifecycle state all passed.
+- Reviewed the source CSS for presentation, natural-height phone/no-JavaScript reading, visible focus, and one-slide-per-page print behavior.
+
+Verification gaps
+
+The browser tool rejected the local file URL under its URL security policy. No alternate route was used to bypass that restriction.
+No slide was visually rendered or inspected at 1440×900 or 390×844. Actual text geometry, clipping, native Tab traversal, no-JavaScript browser reading, screen-reader behavior and printed PDF pages were not tested. The DOM harness verifies JavaScript state, not browser layout or native interaction.
+
+Reproduce the offline checks from the task directory:
+python3 qa/verify.py
+node qa/runtime-check.cjs
